WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
Push a child on a playground swing.

2
00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:05.750
Each push is small and gentle.

3
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.650
Yet push after push, the swing
climbs higher and higher.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:16.460
In 2000, a footbridge in London began to
sway sideways under crowds of walkers.

5
00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.790
It closed after two days.

6
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:24.480
How can small pushes, timed just
right, build up such a huge swing?

7
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:29.110
In this mission, you'll compare a system
left to oscillate freely with one driven

8
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.120
by a repeating force.

9
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.790
Then you'll change how
often the pushes come,

10
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.820
and plot how big the oscillation grows.

11
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain how
small pushes, timed just right,

12
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.230
can build up a huge swing.
